{"skill":{"slug":"credential-manager","displayName":"Credential Manager"},"version":{"version":"1.3.0","createdAt":1770436388201,"changelog":"Consolidation Rule enforcement - all credentials MUST be in ~/.openclaw/.env ONLY. Enhanced detection for workspace/skills/scripts .env files. New CONSOLIDATION-RULE.md documentation.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":5868,"sha256":"dee78166cf01189e2cb82896b78f812cda23fe948e7668a79b339c0ef0f3a376","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CONSOLIDATION-RULE.md","size":2865,"sha256":"8deacc452e0ea3e7b8e5fdbffb748a8620fa4d7259b7fe42bd83bad0dd4f5b76","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CORE-PRINCIPLE.md","size":3914,"sha256":"8c34e6ebfb7b8fbfa4e57aa5183af556292e9c14c92c9c4801f05ada2f61c6ad","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":6722,"sha256":"8ad41842ad7cf2bd22379481d4fccff8df14cf34a84777b923365221fe83de4c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8421,"sha256":"bfbee7fed897c850244e2175281d22c6d47d7713284532e608af0688b0cc5aff","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/security.md","size":4518,"sha256":"3e20fc646eb01f55026c4a53f9d5f11fc3ac05fe995d5d98fdbc973992c5c77e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/supported-services.md","size":4839,"sha256":"0f04331332fc7ba17054c33ea89b918558f74014c137addd4ed66e24f50d5da5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/cleanup.py","size":3840,"sha256":"b185b21700b8eaff224632993bfa3e1b1fd4a23519983cda6a049b4f43511bb1","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/consolidate.py","size":8858,"sha256":"99940901579f9c5e04725530f61f73a42fea501c6498ceca04b94cb8615ff477","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/enforce.py","size":3801,"sha256":"5bbb75af41decbf0d4e20e9467311f8cf4be4ff80f538ac34f9211c18068b347","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/scan.py","size":5340,"sha256":"744711e33482e27736e7dd423f76562d42978d217ee017176043e6863ea58639","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/validate.py","size":6951,"sha256":"1da9a8d3b1c82da681f505ee3cc9a474efb5e19c1aca94d11958d913cff2e9da","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2546,"sha256":"6d37a985e4240cebcec5d1d4ec9f7973a73a06f79d27730ac3508a0814ddd09d","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789035165951,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"935325ba7c37433bfc3783d39adf74ca489f26ee040c0285251770b18ba4dc9d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/935325ba7c37433bfc3783d39adf74ca489f26ee040c0285251770b18ba4dc9d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: credential-manager\nVersion: 1.3.0\n\nThis skill is classified as suspicious due to its extensive use of high-risk capabilities, including scanning the entire filesystem for credential files, reading their contents, modifying sensitive files like `.env` and `.gitignore`, changing file permissions (`chmod 600`), and deleting original credential files. While these actions are explicitly stated as necessary for its security-enhancing purpose (centralizing and securing credentials), they represent significant control over the user's sensitive data and system configuration. The `SKILL.md` and other documentation files use strong, imperative language to instruct the agent to perform these actions, which, while aimed at enforcing security, constitutes a form of prompt injection directing the agent to execute sensitive operations.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161576220},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":147,"checkedAt":1789035165951},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This credential-management skill is purpose-aligned and shows no exfiltration, but it broadly gathers, centralizes, backs up, and can delete sensitive secrets in ways that need careful Review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Default discovery covers broad cross-application locations such as ~/.config/*/credentials.json, ~/.local/share/*/credentials.json, OpenClaw memory files, skill directories, workspace .env files, and custom paths, then reads values and aggregates them without per-file approval.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact contains local Python scripts and Markdown documentation with no observed remote payload retrieval, package installation, install hook, network exfiltration, or obfuscation; users invoke the scripts manually or through documented commands.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions frame consolidation as mandatory with no exceptions, tell other skills to depend on this skill for credential access, and include bash examples that source ~/.openclaw/.env directly, which can execute shell syntax from a tampered or malformed .env file.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persistently writes ~/.openclaw/.env, .env.example, .gitignore, and plaintext backups, and cleanup can permanently unlink original credential files after confirmation without proving each file was successfully migrated and backed up.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is credential consolidation, and the scripts do scan, parse, back up, merge, validate, and clean up credentials; however, the default design intentionally centralizes many high-value secrets, including API tokens, private keys, mnemonics, and seed phrases, into one plaintext file.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to let this skill read and reorganize credentials across your account. Before running consolidation or cleanup, review the exact files it found, avoid --yes for sensitive migrations, protect or encrypt backups yourself, do not store wallet seed phrases or irreplaceable private keys unless you fully accept the risk, and do not delete originals until you have verified the new store and backups work.","findings":"[PE3] expected: Credential access is central to the skill's declared purpose, so the scanner's credential-access signal is not evidence of theft by itself; it remains material because the artifact intentionally scans broad wildcard locations and consolidates unrelated secrets into one plaintext store.\n[TP4] unexpected: I did not accept the claim that the documentation describes functionality absent from the artifact: the inspected scripts do implement scanning, backup, consolidation, validation, and cleanup, although with unsafe edge cases.\n[T05] unexpected: The broad default scan scope is over-provisioned for a credential migration tool because it reads cross-application credential files, OpenClaw memory credential files, and local share credentials without a narrower default allowlist or per-source consent.\n[T09] unexpected: The static scan's backup concern is supported: consolidate.py copies credential files into ~/.openclaw/backups with shutil.copy2 and does not create encrypted backups or explicitly secure backup permissions, conflicting with the artifact's own encrypted-backup guidance.\n[T09] unexpected: The cleanup concern is supported: cleanup.py deletes every discovered old credential file after confirmation but does not verify a current successful migration manifest, equivalent destination contents, or a matching complete backup for each file.\n[T09] unexpected: The git-ignore and shell-loading concerns are supported in part: validation uses substring checks for .env protection, and the docs recommend sourcing ~/.openclaw/.env in bash, which is unsafe for a file containing aggregated secrets from multiple sources.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789035165951}}}}}